  "body": "Hello, in the Navigator and using an azerty keyboard, I can't assign a color label or star rating to thumbnails using the shortcuts Shift+number or Alt+number. Nothing happens. \n\nI also can't use the shortcuts for \"Show only photos with [number] stars\" (shortcuts 1-5 + 0), again nothing happens. \n\nThe shortcut for \"Show only photos with this color label\" (Alt+number) works though. \n\nI guess this has to do with the azerty layout, if I want to type a \"1\", that's done by Shift+1. \n\nEDIT. The above is the case with Xubuntu 24.04. \n\nTried a laptop with Windows 11 today with these results:\n* I can assign a star rating to a thumbnail with Shift+number\n* I can assign a color label using Ctrl+Shift+1-5 but remove a color label with Ctrl-Shift-0 does not work. \n* Show all thumbs with a red label, Alt+1, works.\n* Show all thumbs with x stars works, but without using the Shift key! So the shortcuts on a Azerty keyboard are effectively & é \" ' and ( \n",
